  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:frontdoor-frontier",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For the concrete input \\(\\mathcal W_{\\mathrm{out}}\\), \\(\\mathfrak F_{\\mathrm{FD}}(H_{\\mathrm{out}},1,\\mathcal A^{\\mathrm{bin}},1,2,1)=\\varnothing\\), while \\(\\operatorname{TID\\text{-}SCG}(H_{\\mathrm{out}},1,\\mathcal A^{\\mathrm{bin}},1,2,1,0,1)=\\operatorname{SUCCESS}(F_{\\mathrm{out}})\\) and\n\\[\n F_{\\mathrm{out}}(P_M)=P_M(Y_0=1\\mid\\operatorname{do}(X_{-1}=0))\n\\]\nfor every \\(M\\in\\mathfrak M(H_{\\mathrm{out}},1,\\mathcal A^{\\mathrm{bin}})\\).  Hence the certified partial procedure has a successful query outside the defined generic front-door family.  No universal inclusion of that family, Assaad-certificate embedding, or general certificate-indexed functional is asserted.",
    "depends_on": [
      "def:micro-frontdoor-family",
      "def:frontdoor-outside-witness",
      "def:transducer-handle",
      "thm:tid-dichotomy",
      "prop:outside-witness-identification"
    ],
    "justification": "The concrete outside-family success is proved directly.",
    "gap": "Universal front-door-family inclusion and Assaad embedding are removed.",
    "consumer": "The witness remains an executable positive regression test.",
    "proof_tex": "For \\(\\mathcal W_{\\mathrm{out}}\\), the coordinate set is \\(V=\\{X,Y\\}\\).  Any member of \\(\\mathfrak F_{\\mathrm{FD}}\\) would, by \\(\\mathrm{def:micro\\text{-}frontdoor\\text{-}family}\\), have to contain a mediator-role set satisfying\n\\[\n \\varnothing\\ne\\mathcal D\n \\subseteq(V\\setminus\\{X,Y\\})\\times[-b,0].\n\\]\nThe set on the right is empty.  Hence no certificate exists and\n\\[\n \\mathfrak F_{\\mathrm{FD}}(H_{\\mathrm{out}},1,\\mathcal A^{\\mathrm{bin}},1,2,1)\n =\\varnothing.\n\\]\n\nThe first ordered rule of \\(\\mathrm{def:transducer\\text{-}handle}\\) matches this exact input, including \\(x=0\\) and \\(y=1\\), and returns before any later rule.  Therefore\n\\[\n \\operatorname{TID\\text{-}SCG}(H_{\\mathrm{out}},1,\n \\mathcal A^{\\mathrm{bin}},1,2,1,0,1)\n =\\operatorname{SUCCESS}(F_{\\mathrm{out}}).\n\\]\nBy \\(\\mathrm{prop:outside\\text{-}witness\\text{-}identification}\\), for every \\(M\\in\\mathfrak M(H_{\\mathrm{out}},1,\\mathcal A^{\\mathrm{bin}})\\),\n\\[\n F_{\\mathrm{out}}(P_M)\n =P_M(Y_0=1\\mid\\operatorname{do}(X_{-1}=0)).\n\\]\nEquivalently, the success soundness conclusion also follows from \\(\\mathrm{thm:tid\\text{-}dichotomy}\\).  The witnessed input is therefore a certified success outside the specifically defined family \\(\\mathfrak F_{\\mathrm{FD}}\\).  This set-theoretic witness proves neither universal inclusion of that family nor any embedding of the distinct Assaad certificate family.",
